<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George II Rákóczi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1621">1621</a>–<a href="/years/1660">1660</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George II Rákóczi was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-transylvania">Prince of Transylvania</a> from 1648. Seeking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Polish crown</a>, he invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in 1657 in alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> without Ottoman permission; his army was destroyed, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-tatars">Crimean Tatars</a> ravaged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> in reprisal. Deposed by the sultan, he fought on to regain power and died of wounds received in battle in 1660.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-ii-rakoczi.jpg" alt="George II Rákóczi" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:I.r%C3%A1k%C3%B3czi_gy%C3%B6rgy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
